# Frontend structure (layers + features)

Organize Vue code under `src/` by **layer** (shared) and **feature** (domain). Do not dump domain logic into `App.vue` or flat folders.

## Layout

```
src/
├── main.ts, App.vue          # bootstrap + root shell only
├── assets/, styles/          # static assets, global CSS
├── components/               # reusable UI (no domain logic)
│   ├── ui/                   # Naive UI wrappers if needed
│   └── layout/               # AppShell, Sidebar, Toolbar
├── features/<name>/          # domain slices (request, response, …)
│   ├── components/
│   ├── composables/
│   └── types.ts              # feature-local types only
├── stores/                   # Pinia — one store per domain
├── composables/              # shared hooks (cross-feature)
├── services/                 # Tauri invoke / I/O only
├── types/                    # shared contracts
└── utils/                    # pure helpers (no Vue, no Tauri)
```

## Rules

1. **`App.vue`** composes layout only — no HTTP / Tauri / business logic.
2. **Domain UI** lives in `features/<name>/`, not in root `components/`.
3. **`components/`** = generic, reusable. If removing the feature would make the component meaningless, it belongs in that feature.
4. **Tauri / `invoke`** only in `services/`. Components and stores call services, never `@tauri-apps/api` directly.
5. **Features do not import each other deeply.** Shared code goes to `components/`, `composables/`, `stores/`, `types/`, or `utils/`.
6. **One Pinia store per domain** (`stores/request.ts`, not a mega-store).
7. Prefer `@/` imports (e.g. `@/services/http`). Do not create empty folders “for later”.

## Example — send a request

```
✅ GOOD
features/request/components/RequestUrlBar.vue  → calls store action
stores/request.ts                              → calls service
services/http.ts                               → invoke('send_request', …)
types/http.ts                                  → RequestDraft, HttpResponse

❌ BAD
App.vue                    → invoke(...) + parse body + update UI
components/RequestUrlBar.vue → import { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/core'
features/response/…        → import from features/request/… (cross-feature)
```

When adding UI for a new domain area (history, collections, environments), create `features/<name>/` and a matching store if state is shared — do not append it to an unrelated feature or to `App.vue`.
